+          "quote": "Input a real active column $x\\in\\mathbb F^r$ and trailing block $B\\in\\mathbb F^{r\\times q}$ with entries in the floating-point system, $r\\ge1$, $q\\ge0$. If every component of $x$ is zero, return the identity action and a copy of $B$, with the active output column set to exact zeros, so that $C_+=[0e_1\\;B]$; return $(v=0,\\widehat\\tau=0,\\widehat\\alpha=0,C_+)$ marked `identity`. Otherwise compute $s=\\max_{1\\le i\\le r}|x_i|>0$, and then, in increasing $i$, compute $z_i=\\operatorname{fl}(x_i/s)$. Initialize $t=0$ and, in increasing $i$, compute $a_i=\\operatorname{fl}(z_i z_i)$ followed by $t=\\operatorname{fl}(t+a_i)$. Compute $h=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sqrt t)$ and then $\\widehat r=\\operatorname{fl}(s h)$. Set $\\sigma=1$ if $x_1=0$ and $\\sigma=\\operatorname{sign}(x_1)$ otherwise, and set $\\widehat\\alpha=-\\sigma\\widehat r$ using the exact sign change. Compute $v_1=\\operatorname{fl}(x_1-\\widehat\\alpha)$, then copy $v_i=x_i$ exactly for $i=2,\\ldots,r$.\n\nInitialize $w=0$ and, in increasing $i$, compute $a_i=\\operatorname{fl}(v_i v_i)$ followed by $w=\\operatorname{fl}(w+a_i)$. Then compute $\\widehat\\tau=\\operatorname{fl}(2/w)$. For each column $j=1,\\ldots,q$ in increasing order, initialize $d_j=0$ and, in increasing $i$, compute $a_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(v_i B_{ij})$ followed by $d_j=\\operatorname{fl}(d_j+a_{ij})$. After all $d_j$ have been computed, in increasing $i$ compute $p_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\widehat\\tau v_i)$. Then, in increasing $j$ and within each column in increasing $i$, compute $U_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(p_i d_j)$ and $\\widehat B_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}(B_{ij}-U_{ij})$ in that order. The complete active output is $C_+=[\\widehat\\alpha e_1\\;\\widehat B]$, with exact zeros written below its first diagonal entry. If any elementary operation fails, return the first range failure with its stage and indices in the order above. Also return failure if $t$, $\\widehat r$, or $w$ is not positive normal, or an