-          "quote": "Input nonsingular real $A\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$, $n\\ge1$, and $b,x_0\\in\\mathbb R^n$, nonsingular factor matrix $\\widehat A$ formed at factorization precision $u_f$, residual precision $u_r$, solve/update precision $u_w$, finite budget $N\\ge0$, tolerance $\\tau\\ge0$, certified nonnegative constants $\\eta_r,\\xi_r,\\eta_w,\\xi_w$, and a certified contraction upper bound $0\\le q_{\\mathrm{cert}}<1$. Let $x_*=A^{-1}b$ be the unique exact solution. Use the operationwise model of [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]] separately at $u_f,u_r,u_w$. The exact data $A,b$ are available to residual evaluation at $u_r$; stored iterates and correction updates use $u_w$. At iteration $k$, compute $\\widehat r_k=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_r}(b-Ax_k)$, solve for a correction using the supplied triangular factors of $\\widehat A$ and the recurrence in [[def-forward-and-back-substitution-for-triangular-systems]], then round $x_{k+1}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(x_k+\\widehat z_k)$. A certificate must bound the residual defect $\\widehat r_k=A(x_*-x_k)+\\delta_{r,k}$ by $\\|\\delta_{r,k}\\|_2\\le\\eta_r(\\|A\\|_2\\|x_k\\|_2+\\|b\\|_2)+\\xi_r$, and the combined solve/update residual-equivalent error is defined by\n$$x_{k+1}=x_k+\\widehat A^{-1}(\\widehat r_k+\\delta_{w,k}),\\qquad \\|\\delta_{w,k}\\|_2\\le\\eta_w\\|\\widehat r_k\\|_2+\\xi_w.$$\nThe certificate must verify that $q\\le q_{\\mathrm{cert}}$, where\n$$q=\\|I-\\widehat A^{-1}A\\|_2+ \\|\\widehat A^{-1}\\|_2((1+\\eta_w)\\eta_r+\\eta_w)\\|A\\|_2.$$\nIf a required range or nonsingularity check fails, a certificate is unavailable, or $q\\le q_{\\mathrm{cert}}<1$ is not certified, return inconclusive. Otherwise test the current residual, return residual-tolerance if its computed norm is at most $\\tau$, and update at most $N$ times; return budget-exhausted after $N$ unsuccessful updates. Return the current iterate with its status. The procedure is finite and does not claim exact termination or unconditional convergence.",
+          "quote": "Input nonsingular real $A\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$, $n\\ge1$, exact data $b\\in\\mathbb R^n$, and an initial iterate $x_0$ stored at solve/update precision $u_w$. Also input stored triangular factors $\\widehat L,\\widehat U$ formed at factorization precision $u_f$, where $\\widehat L$ is lower triangular, $\\widehat U$ is upper triangular, both have nonzero diagonals, and $\\widehat A:=\\widehat L\\widehat U$ is the exact real product; thus $\\widehat A$ is nonsingular. Input residual precision $u_r$, solve/update precision $u_w$, finite update budget $N\\ge0$, tolerance $\\tau\\ge0$, a stagnation window $K_{\\rm stag}\\ge1$, certified nonnegative constants $\\eta_r,\\xi_r,\\eta_w,\\xi_w$, and a certified contraction upper bound $0\\le q_{\\rm cert}<1$. Let $x_*=A^{-1}b$. Use the operationwise model of [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]] at each stated precision. Entries of the exact data $A,b$ are available as real operands to the residual operations; the stored factors, iterates, residuals, and corrections are used as their exact represented values in those operations.\n\nBefore iterating, check the factor conditions and a supplied certificate establishing $q\\le q_{\\rm cert}<1$, where\n$$q=\\|I-\\widehat A^{-1}A\\|_2+\\|\\widehat A^{-1}\\|_2\\bigl((1+\\eta_w)\\eta_r+\\eta_w\\bigr)\\|A\\|_2.$$\nThe certificate must include certified norm bounds sufficient to verify this inequality; an unavailable or unverified certificate returns `inconclusive` with $x_0$.\n\nBefore entering the iteration loop, initialize the consecutive-equality counter $c_{\\rm stag}=0$ and mark the preceding residual as undefined. Retain this counter and preceding residual across iterations; do not reinitialize them inside the loop. The counter records the number of consecutive equalities between adjacent successfully certified computed residual vectors.\n\nFor each $k=0,\\ldots,N$, compute the residual by rows in increasing $i$: initialize $s_i=0$, then for $j=1,\\ldots,n$ in increasing order compute $p_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_r}(A_{ij}x_{k,j})$ and $s_i=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_r}(s_i+p_{ij})$; finally set $\\widehat r_{k,i}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_r}(b_i-s_i)$. Any operationwise range failure returns `inconclusive` with the current iterate and the first failing row, column, and operation. Define the exact residual defect $\\delta_{r,k}=\\widehat r_k-(b-Ax_k)$, so $\\widehat r_k=A(x_*-x_k)+\\delta_{r,k}$. A supplied per-iteration certificate must establish\n$$\\|\\delta_{r,k}\\|_2\\le\\eta_r(\\|A\\|_2\\|x_k\\|_2+\\|b\\|_2)+\\xi_r.$$\nIf it is unavailable or cannot be verified from certified norm bounds, return `inconclusive` with the current iterate.\n\nUse the retained consecutive-equality counter and preceding residual. Use the exact Euclidean norm of the stored residual vector for the status comparison; this is a comparison of the already computed vector, not an additional rounded arithmetic operation. If $\\|\\widehat r_k\\|_2\\le\\tau$, return `residual-tolerance` with $x_k$. If a preceding residual exists, compare its components exactly with those of $\\widehat r_k$: if all are equal, increment $c_{\\rm stag}$ by one; otherwise reset it to zero. If $c_{\\rm stag}=K_{\\rm stag}$, return `successful-stagnation` with $x_k$. This status certifies only that the last $K_{\\rm stag}$ successful updates produced identical computed residual vectors, with all range and contraction certificates accepted; it certifies neither a small exact error nor convergence. Before any further update, store $\\widehat r_k$ as the preceding residual.\n\nIf $k=N$ and neither status above was returned, return `budget-exhausted` with $x_k$. Otherwise solve $\\widehat L y_k=\\widehat r_k$ by forward substitution, then $\\widehat U\\widehat z_k=y_k$ by backward substitution, using precision $u_w$. For forward substitution, visit rows $i=1,\\ldots,n$ in increasing order, initialize $s_i=0$, and for $j=1,\\ldots,i-1$ in increasing order compute $p_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(\\widehat L_{ij}y_{k,j})$ and $s_i=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(s_i+p_{ij})$, then $t_i=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(\\widehat r_{k,i}-s_i)$ and $y_{k,i}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(t_i/\\widehat L_{ii})$. For backward substitution, visit rows $i=n,\\ldots,1$ in decreasing order, initialize $s_i=0$, and for $j=i+1,\\ldots,n$ in increasing order compute $p_{ij}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(\\widehat U_{ij}\\widehat z_{k,j})$ and $s_i=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(s_i+p_{ij})$, then $t_i=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(y_{k,i}-s_i)$ and $\\widehat z_{k,i}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(t_i/\\widehat U_{ii})$. Update components in increasing order by $x_{k+1,i}=\\operatorname{fl}_{u_w}(x_{k,i}+\\widehat z_{k,i})$. A failed operation returns `inconclusive` with the current iterate and first failing operation location.\n\nAfter a successful update, define the exact residual-equivalent update defect\n$$\\delta_{w,k}:=\\widehat A(x_{k+1}-x_k)-\\widehat r_k,$$\nso $x_{k+1}=x_k+\\widehat A^{-1}(\\widehat r_k+\\delta_{w,k})$. A supplied per-iteration certificate must establish $\\|\\delta_{w,k}\\|_2\\le\\eta_w\\|\\widehat r_k\\|_2+\\xi_w$; if unavailable or unverified, return `inconclusive` with $x_{k+1}$. Continue until one of the stated statuses is returned. All loops are finite. The procedure does not claim exact termination or unconditional convergence.",
