-          "quote": "Let $R\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be upper triangular with nonzero diagonal, $y\\in\\mathbb R^n$, $n\\ge1$, and $(n+3)u<1$. Compute descending substitution by the sequential rounded dot $s_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sum_{j>i}R_{ij}\\widehat x_j)$ (empty sum zero), $t_i=\\operatorname{fl}(y_i-s_i)$, and $\\widehat x_i=\\operatorname{fl}(t_i/R_{ii})$. If every operation succeeds, there is upper triangular $\\Delta R$ with\n$$(R+\\Delta R)\\widehat x=y,\\qquad |\\Delta R|\\le\\gamma_{n+3}|R|,\\qquad \\|\\Delta R\\|_F\\le\\gamma_{n+3}\\|R\\|_F.$$\nIn particular $\\widehat x=0$ forces $y=0$. Forward substitution has the transposed conclusion.",
+          "quote": "Let $R\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be upper triangular with stored floating-point entries and nonzero diagonal, and let $y\\in\\mathbb R^n$ have stored floating-point entries, where $n\\ge1$ and $(n+3)u<1$. Use the operationwise arithmetic model of [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]] at unit roundoff $u$. Compute descending substitution by the sequential rounded dot $s_i=\\operatorname{fl}(\\sum_{j>i}R_{ij}\\widehat x_j)$ (empty sum zero), $t_i=\\operatorname{fl}(y_i-s_i)$, and $\\widehat x_i=\\operatorname{fl}(t_i/R_{ii})$. Assume each exact intermediate is zero or normal and each rounded result is finite, so every operation succeeds under that model. Then there is upper triangular $\\Delta R$ with\n$$(R+\\Delta R)\\widehat x=y,\\qquad |\\Delta R|\\le\\gamma_{n+3}|R|,\\qquad \\|\\Delta R\\|_F\\le\\gamma_{n+3}\\|R\\|_F.$$\nIn particular $\\widehat x=0$ forces $y=0$. Forward substitution has the transposed conclusion.",
