-          "quote": "Input real floating-point x_1,...,x_n, n>=1. Set d=ceil(log_2 n), append 2^d-n exact zero leaves, and round the sum at each internal node of the balanced tree. An unmatched leaf may be copied. If a rounded node fails the operationwise range rule, return range-failure and its tree index; otherwise return the root s-hat. This finite tree terminates after 2^d-1 additions; accuracy is asserted only on success.",
+          "quote": "Input real floating-point values $x_1,\\ldots,x_n$, $n\\ge1$. Set $d=\\lceil\\log_2 n\\rceil$, place these values in leaves $1,\\ldots,n$ from left to right, and append $2^d-n$ exact zero leaves. At level $\\ell=1,\\ldots,d$, replace each consecutive pair of current nodes $(a_{\\ell-1,2j-1},a_{\\ell-1,2j})$, in increasing $j=1,\\ldots,2^{d-\\ell}$, by\n$$a_{\\ell,j}=\\operatorname{fl}(a_{\\ell-1,2j-1}+a_{\\ell-1,2j}).$$\nIf an operation fails, return `range-failure` with the first failing level $\\ell$ and node $j$ in this level-by-level, left-to-right order. For $d=0$, return $x_1$ with no additions. Otherwise return the single node $a_{d,1}$. The tree is fully specified, terminates after $2^d-1$ additions, and its accuracy is asserted only on success.",
